  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Given a square with side of length \\(s.\\) On a diagonal as base a triangle with three unequal sides is constructed so that its area equals that of the square. The length of the altitude drawn to the base is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(s\\sqrt2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{s}{\\sqrt2}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(2s\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(2\\sqrt{s}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac2{\\sqrt{s}}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1964-p10.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The triangle’s base is the square’s diagonal, \\(s\\sqrt2.\\) If its altitude is \\(h,\\) equality of areas gives \\[\\frac12(s\\sqrt2)h=s^2,\\] so \\(h=s\\sqrt2.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "The square’s diagonal has length \\(s\\sqrt2\\)",
        "Set \\(\\frac12(s\\sqrt2)h=s^2\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
